    "summary": "A woman&#039;s bib / plastron; part of festive attire.  Made from a rectangular piece of natural cream twill woven cloth gathered onto a blue cotton velvet neckband.  Decoration in a &#039;V&#039; shape at the middle top of plastron: small transparent, blue, green and red glass beads, gold and black faceted beads, a line of silver-coloured metal sequins, blue and black rickrack and polychrome tubular glass beads.  The neckband is similarly decorated and is fastened with a blue domed plastic button and green cotton braided loop.",
